WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.367
-Sebastian, welcome back.

00:00:02.367 --> 00:00:04.000
-Oh, good to be here.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:06.667
Great crowd, great band,
great host.

00:00:06.667 --> 00:00:10.534
-Oh, my God. That's what I'm --
You look sharp.

00:00:10.534 --> 00:00:12.033
You look great.

00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:15.167
By the way, backstage, I noticed
you don't have an entourage.

00:00:15.167 --> 00:00:18.667
-No, I come solo
to these things.

00:00:18.667 --> 00:00:20.601
There's a lot going on
back there.

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:23.334
A lot of people bringing
a lot -- 30, 35 people.

00:00:23.334 --> 00:00:28.234
And I look at that, and I go,
"Every head is cash."

00:00:28.234 --> 00:00:29.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:29.634 --> 00:00:31.834
-That's -- Yeah, that's right.
Okay, I see. Yeah.

00:00:31.834 --> 00:00:33.701
So, you don't mess with that.

00:00:33.701 --> 00:00:35.634
Can I just tell you how great,
by the way --

00:00:35.634 --> 00:00:37.834
The special is fantastic.
-Thank you.

00:00:37.834 --> 00:00:39.534
-"Is It Me?"
You got to watch.

00:00:39.534 --> 00:00:41.767
And we'll get into that.
But also, just all of

00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:43.334
what you've done
in your whole comedy.

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:44.801
I was going to send you this.

00:00:44.801 --> 00:00:47.501
I was telling you backstage,
there's kids -- This one kid is

00:00:47.501 --> 00:00:50.968
doing an impression of you so
good, a fantastic impression.

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:52.701
I go, "I'm going to send that
to Sebastian."

00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:55.234
And then I flipped and I saw
another kid doing you.

00:00:55.234 --> 00:00:56.667
And then there's like
thousands of people.

00:00:56.667 --> 00:00:57.934
Everyone's --
Does that feel good

00:00:57.934 --> 00:00:59.033
when people do impressions
of you?

00:00:59.033 --> 00:00:59.968
-No.

00:00:59.968 --> 00:01:01.367
[ Laughter ]

00:01:01.367 --> 00:01:03.067
-You don't like it.
-No, it's flattery.

00:01:03.067 --> 00:01:05.367
I like it.
-I mean, this is it.

00:01:05.367 --> 00:01:06.801
-Yeah, no, it's nice, man.

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:07.968
I never thought I'd get
to this point.

00:01:07.968 --> 00:01:09.033
I never thought I'd be
sitting here

00:01:09.033 --> 00:01:10.801
talking to you on
"The Fallon Show."

00:01:10.801 --> 00:01:12.067
I mean, come on.
-Oh, come on, buddy.

00:01:12.067 --> 00:01:13.801
I'm so happy.
I'm thankful you're here.

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:15.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:15.100 --> 00:01:16.734
And you're here
during the holidays.

00:01:16.734 --> 00:01:18.801
-Love it.
-How was your Thanksgiving?

00:01:18.801 --> 00:01:20.767
-So, let me tell you about
Thanksgiving.

00:01:20.767 --> 00:01:22.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:26.834
I don't like when people make
food at their house

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:30.834
and then bring it to my house.

00:01:30.834 --> 00:01:32.300
Right?
-Uh-huh. I understand.

00:01:32.300 --> 00:01:35.234
-It's always leaking, you know?

00:01:35.234 --> 00:01:36.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.434 --> 00:01:39.901
There's, like, a trail
from their car

00:01:39.901 --> 00:01:42.234
to my kitchen.
-Okay.

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:46.734
-And it's always unidentifiable.

00:01:46.734 --> 00:01:49.200
They got to explain what it is.

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:52.334
They're like,
"It's a family recipe."

00:01:52.334 --> 00:01:54.067
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.067 --> 00:01:58.133
"It's a little cinnamon,
pecan, chicken --"

00:01:58.133 --> 00:01:59.467
Chicken?

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:02.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:03.667
I'm always wondering
where to put it.

00:02:03.667 --> 00:02:05.501
I'm like, "Put it
near the garbage."

00:02:05.501 --> 00:02:07.167
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:09.334
-That's the close place
to put it. Yeah.

00:02:09.334 --> 00:02:11.667
But are you in
the Christmas spirit here?

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:14.234
-I am in the Christmas spirit.

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:19.133
I'm making eggnog this Saturday.

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:21.100
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:23.067
For a --

00:02:23.067 --> 00:02:26.767
Yeah, so, we're going to have
a party Saturday at the house.

00:02:26.767 --> 00:02:29.901
Right?
I wanted it small -- 14 people.

00:02:29.901 --> 00:02:31.467
I'm going to make
a little eggnog,

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:32.901
have the people come over.

00:02:32.901 --> 00:02:38.300
But my wife, it's ballooned to
65 people, alright?

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:40.934
Now, the recipe only goes to 14.

00:02:40.934 --> 00:02:43.834
So I don't know what I'm going
to do now that there's 60.

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:48.467
And it's ballooned where --
My wife is so creative.

00:02:48.467 --> 00:02:51.701
She's an artist. She's like,
"What if we get a reindeer?"

00:02:51.701 --> 00:02:55.000
[ Laughter ]

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.734
-So -- Yeah.
-Wow.

00:02:56.734 --> 00:02:57.767
Like a real -- a reindeer?

00:02:57.767 --> 00:02:59.701
-Yeah, she wants -- Listen.

00:02:59.701 --> 00:03:02.701
We've had these parties, these
elaborate parties, and listen.

00:03:02.701 --> 00:03:04.501
I'm from the Midwest.
I'm very --

00:03:04.501 --> 00:03:06.701
[ Cheers ]
Yeah, from Chicago.

00:03:06.701 --> 00:03:09.234
Our parties were very simple
growing up.

00:03:09.234 --> 00:03:10.567
Played games.

00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:12.000
There was nothing --
-Yeah.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:13.767
-Nothing too --
-Fanfare.

00:03:13.767 --> 00:03:14.934
You don't need a big thing.
-No.

00:03:14.934 --> 00:03:16.200
But my wife, she's got to be --

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.033
"What about a Santa
on the roof?"

00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:21.534
We're not getting
a Santa on the roof!

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:24.834
[ Laughter ]

00:03:24.834 --> 00:03:26.267
-But do the kids like it?

00:03:26.267 --> 00:03:28.501
How old are the kids?
-It's not even a kiddy party.

00:03:28.501 --> 00:03:30.000
This is adults.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:31.834
-This is --
You're having eggnog.

00:03:31.834 --> 00:03:33.701
-Eggnog for 65 adults,

00:03:33.701 --> 00:03:36.767
and my wife wants a reindeer
walking around in the yard.

00:03:36.767 --> 00:03:39.133
So I said -- I had to put a --

00:03:39.133 --> 00:03:40.968
-Walking around in the yard.
-Yeah.

00:03:40.968 --> 00:03:42.968
-How old are the kids?

00:03:42.968 --> 00:03:47.367
-They're 5 and they're 3
and I'm 49.

00:03:47.367 --> 00:03:51.968
And that's a 46-year gap.

00:03:51.968 --> 00:03:53.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:54.701
And for the older parents
out there,

00:03:54.701 --> 00:03:57.267
you start doing math
if you're older, you know?

00:03:57.267 --> 00:04:00.534
I could very well be
in a wheelchair

00:04:00.534 --> 00:04:02.567
at my daughter's wedding, right?

00:04:02.567 --> 00:04:05.167
-Oh, my God.
-They'll just wheel me in.

00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:06.834
There will be
a 10-minute discussion.

00:04:06.834 --> 00:04:08.334
"Where do you want to put Dad?"

00:04:08.334 --> 00:04:10.200
[ Laughter ]

00:04:10.200 --> 00:04:12.167
-"Where do you want to put Dad?"

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:14.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.067 --> 00:04:15.701
"Where do you want to put Dad?"

00:04:15.701 --> 00:04:18.133
-Yeah.
-That's hilarious.

00:04:18.133 --> 00:04:21.234
You've had a great
stand-up career.

00:04:21.234 --> 00:04:25.033
You've sold out Madison Square
Garden multiple nights.

00:04:25.033 --> 00:04:26.267
Radio City --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:26.267 --> 00:04:28.767
-Thank you.
-It's like it's nothing.

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:31.801
Do you remember one of the worst
gigs that you played?

00:04:31.801 --> 00:04:34.400
-Worst gigs?

00:04:34.400 --> 00:04:38.667
It was in Manteca, California.

00:04:38.667 --> 00:04:41.100
And it was a boxing ring.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:44.467
Now, the problem with stand-up,
people think they can just

00:04:44.467 --> 00:04:46.934
throw it up anywhere
and it's going to work.

00:04:46.934 --> 00:04:49.801
So, we walked in and I asked
the guy, "Where's the stage?"

00:04:49.801 --> 00:04:52.167
He goes,
"Well, it's the boxing ring."

00:04:52.167 --> 00:04:53.968
I said, "Alright."

00:04:53.968 --> 00:04:56.100
Now, on top of that,

00:04:56.100 --> 00:05:00.434
there was a bowling alley
behind the boxing ring.

00:05:00.434 --> 00:05:04.567
So, I'm doing jokes
while somebody behind me

00:05:04.567 --> 00:05:06.667
is trying to pick up a spare,
alright?

00:05:06.667 --> 00:05:08.100
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:11.734
Doesn't really work well in
stand-up when you've got bowling

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:15.067
and blood on the floor
of the stage.

00:05:15.067 --> 00:05:18.534
-No way. I love those gigs.
I remember that.

00:05:18.534 --> 00:05:20.868
I remember there was one
restaurant that started.

00:05:20.868 --> 00:05:23.300
They just go, "Let's just have
comedy night in the restaurant."

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:26.167
-Yeah, just throw it up.
-And I just started doing

00:05:26.167 --> 00:05:28.300
stand-up in the middle of the --
People are just eating.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.667
People are ordering hot wings,

00:05:29.667 --> 00:05:31.634
and I'm going like --
I'm doing my act.

00:05:31.634 --> 00:05:33.601
It was terrible.
-No introduction.

00:05:33.601 --> 00:05:36.033
-No.
-They're like, "Go up."

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:38.300
I'm like, "No introduction?
No nothing?"

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:42.300
And I'm on a milk crate doing
jokes while people are --

00:05:42.300 --> 00:05:44.267
-Do you ever do the gigs where
they don't have a microphone?

00:05:44.267 --> 00:05:47.033
-Oh, yeah, yeah. "Just yell."

00:05:47.033 --> 00:05:48.801
-"Just yell." Exactly, yeah.

00:05:48.801 --> 00:05:50.033
"We'll have everyone be quiet."

00:05:50.033 --> 00:05:51.400
I go, "I don't want everyone
to be quiet.

00:05:51.400 --> 00:05:53.400
It's a stand-up show."
-Awful. It's awful.

00:05:53.400 --> 00:05:55.000
-So, then you do your special
now, which,

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:56.367
by the way, I love the look.

00:05:56.367 --> 00:05:58.801
I mean, you're in Vegas.
You got the tuxedo.

00:05:58.801 --> 00:06:01.834
It's called "Sebastian
Maniscalco: Is It Me?"

00:06:01.834 --> 00:06:04.133
Did you want to do like a whole
Rat Pack-y type of vibe?

00:06:04.133 --> 00:06:06.567
-Yeah, I wanted a throwback
to the Rat Pack where

00:06:06.567 --> 00:06:09.534
people, when they went out,
dressed up, had a tuxedo on.

00:06:09.534 --> 00:06:11.434
I asked the audience
to dress up.

00:06:11.434 --> 00:06:13.601
About 20 people did. Nice.

00:06:13.601 --> 00:06:15.400
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:18.634
I just wanted to do a throwback
because, you know, entertainment

00:06:18.634 --> 00:06:20.834
back then seemed a little bit
more classy.

00:06:20.834 --> 00:06:22.601
Bow tie, you know,
the whole thing.

00:06:22.601 --> 00:06:25.834
So, that -- I gave it a little
nod to the Pack.

00:06:25.834 --> 00:06:27.834
-Did you like Vegas?
Did you like playing Las Vegas?

00:06:27.834 --> 00:06:30.200
-I like it.
You know, cross section between,

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:31.968
you know --
I like the Wynn Hotel.

00:06:31.968 --> 00:06:33.334
That's where I like to perform.

00:06:33.334 --> 00:06:34.734
It's got a nice vibe there.

00:06:34.734 --> 00:06:36.434
Although Vegas has changed.

00:06:36.434 --> 00:06:39.400
You know, I mean, you used to go
to the pool and lay out.

00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:41.467
Now, you go to the pool
and you can't even get in.

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:42.567
I'm like,
"I just want to lay out."

00:06:42.567 --> 00:06:44.133
They're like, "It's going to be
8 grand."

00:06:44.133 --> 00:06:45.868
[ Laughter ]

00:06:45.868 --> 00:06:47.234
-Just to lay out at the pool.

00:06:47.234 --> 00:06:49.467
-To lay out on a lily pad
in the pool.

00:06:49.467 --> 00:06:50.701
[ Laughter ]

00:06:50.701 --> 00:06:53.133
-The title, you ask the
question, "Is it me?"

00:06:53.133 --> 00:06:54.667
-Yeah.

00:06:54.667 --> 00:06:57.300
-Is this based on something that
happens in your real life?

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:01.367
-Well, I constantly walk around
and look at today's environment,

00:07:01.367 --> 00:07:04.701
and I go, "Is it me or...?"

00:07:04.701 --> 00:07:06.934
[ Laughter ]

00:07:06.934 --> 00:07:10.667
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:10.667 --> 00:07:12.067
-People can relate.

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:17.734
But is it you?
Do you think it is us?

00:07:19.067 --> 00:07:21.167
-The more and more I go
throughout the country,

00:07:21.167 --> 00:07:23.868
I'm finding a lot of people are
agreeing with me.

00:07:23.868 --> 00:07:25.000
[ Laughter ]

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:26.767
-Yeah. It's not just you.
-It's not just me.

00:07:26.767 --> 00:07:28.767
-There's many more, yeah.
I want to show a little bit.

00:07:28.767 --> 00:07:30.968
Here's "Sebastian Maniscalco:
Is It Me?"

00:07:30.968 --> 00:07:32.334
Take a look at this special.

00:07:32.334 --> 00:07:36.300
-So, the alarm went off
last month.

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:38.400
And my wife don't get up.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:39.734
I'm up right away.

00:07:39.734 --> 00:07:41.267
And I'm not one of these guys

00:07:41.267 --> 00:07:43.901
that goes and handles it,
alright?

00:07:43.901 --> 00:07:46.334
I'm like, "Get up. Get up!"

00:07:46.334 --> 00:07:55.801
[ Laughter ]

00:07:55.801 --> 00:07:57.834
She's like, "What?
What's going on?"

00:07:57.834 --> 00:08:01.334
I said, "The alarm.
The alarm's on!"

00:08:01.334 --> 00:08:03.000
She's like, "Oh, just go look."

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.400
Yeah, what? I'm going to go
look, take two to the head

00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:08.133
while you escape out the back
with our two kids

00:08:08.133 --> 00:08:10.267
and start another family with
some other guy.

00:08:10.267 --> 00:08:12.133
[Bleep] that. Get on my back.

00:08:12.133 --> 00:08:14.033
We're going out together.

00:08:14.033 --> 00:08:15.400
"Go look."

00:08:15.400 --> 00:08:16.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:08:16.667 --> 00:08:18.634
The hell you think you married?

00:08:18.634 --> 00:08:19.868
Rambo?

00:08:19.868 --> 00:08:21.434
Let's go together.

00:08:23.567 --> 00:08:24.968
-Start another family.

00:08:24.968 --> 00:08:26.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:26.634 --> 00:08:29.667
Come on!
Sebastian Maniscalco, everybody!

00:08:29.667 --> 00:08:33.767
His stand-up special premieres
tomorrow globally on Netflix.

00:08:33.767 --> 00:08:35.801
Beabadoobee performs
after the break.

00:08:35.801 --> 00:08:37.467
Stick around, everybody.
Come on back.

